  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
    "arabic_text": "عَلِيٌّ عَنْ أَبِيهِ عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِي عُمَيْرٍ عَنْ حَمَّادٍ عَنِ الْحَلَبِيِّ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام )",
    "translations": {
      "en": "Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al-Halabi, from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him)"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_type": "body",
    "arabic_text": "فِي الْأَعْمَى يَؤُمُّ الْقَوْمَ وَ هُوَ عَلَى غَيْرِ الْقِبْلَةِ قَالَ يُعِيدُ وَ لَا يُعِيدُونَ فَإِنَّهُمْ قَدْ تَحَرَّوْا",
    "translations": {
      "en": "Regarding the blind man leading the people in prayer while he is facing other than the Qiblah, he (peace be upon him) said: 'He should repeat (his prayer) and they will not be repeating, for they had investigated (the direction of the Qiblah).'"
    }
  },
